            H3("5S"),
            "5S organises the workplace so that problems and abnormalities are obvious at a glance. The five Japanese words and their usual English equivalents are seiri (sort: remove what is not needed), seiton (set in order: a place for everything), seiso (shine: clean and inspect), seiketsu (standardise: make the first three routine) and shitsuke (sustain: keep the discipline). Many organisations add safety as a sixth S. Our guide to [visual management](/project-management/kanban/visual-management/) covers 5S alongside other visual controls.",
